WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.020
At the end of Matthew's Gospel, Jesus
sends his followers out to baptise.

2
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.400
They are to baptise in
the name of the Father,

3
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:10.130
and of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit.

4
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.020
Yet Christians also hold to the
ancient words of Deuteronomy:

5
00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.920
The LORD is one.

6
00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:19.060
And the word Trinity appears
nowhere in the Bible.

7
00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:21.680
So how can that still be one God?

8
00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:26.170
In this mission, you'll trace the idea
from the Bible to the creeds of Nicaea

9
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.840
and Constantinople.

10
00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:32.810
Then you'll see the words the council
of 381 chose for the Holy Spirit.

11
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:36.560
Your mission: find out how
Christians explain that Father,

12
00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:39.390
Son and Holy Spirit are one God.
